finding-amd-power-profile-advice = VR load comes in short bursts and the default profile lets the clocks fall between them, so some frames miss the headset deadline. SteamVR switches to the VR profile itself, WiVRn and Monado do not. Until reboot: echo { $profile } | sudo tee { $file }, or set it permanently in LACT or CoreCtrl.
finding-amd-power-profile-title = The AMD GPU is not in its VR power profile
finding-compositor-not-realtime-advice = When the CPU is busy the compositor misses its deadline and the headset rate halves (90 to 45 or lower) for a while. Grant it once, then restart it: sudo setcap CAP_SYS_NICE=+ep { $path }. A package update removes it.
finding-compositor-not-realtime-title = { $compositor } cannot run its compositor at realtime priority
finding-desktop-entry-missing-advice = A repair recreates it.
finding-desktop-entry-missing-title = The start-menu entry is missing
finding-dips-advice = Neither the GPU load nor its clock explains them, or MangoHud did not report them. They usually come from loading on the game's main thread: worlds, avatars joining, videos.
finding-dips-gpu-bound-advice = Lower the resolution in WiVRn or the in-game graphics settings, or hide distant avatars.
finding-dips-gpu-bound-title = The GPU is saturated during the slowdowns
finding-dips-gpu-clock-advice = Power management lowers the clock just when frames need it. Use the VR power profile (see above) or a fixed performance level.
finding-dips-gpu-clock-title = The GPU clock drops during the slowdowns
finding-dips-gpu-waiting-advice = Frames are late without the GPU being busy: the game's main thread, the compositor or loading (avatars, worlds, video) holds them back. Check the findings above first; a scene with many avatars on a 6-core CPU is the usual limit.
finding-dips-gpu-waiting-title = The GPU idles during the slowdowns
finding-dips-title = Slowdowns in the last session
finding-flatpak-advice = Proton's container cannot start from inside Flatpak without host access. Use the AppImage or the native package.
finding-flatpak-title = Unilux is running inside a Flatpak sandbox
finding-freezes-advice = Irregular freezes usually line up with loading: worlds, avatars joining, videos.
finding-freezes-periodic-advice = Freezes on a fixed clock come from a timer inside the game (a periodic cleanup, a poll, a network or voice task), not from the GPU or the compositor. Note what you were doing and compare with voice chat or the microphone off.
finding-freezes-periodic-title = The game freezes every { $period } s
finding-freezes-title = Freezes in the last session
finding-game-running-title = Somnium Space is running ({ $count } processes)
finding-github-unreachable-advice = Installs and repairs download from GitHub. Check your connection, proxy or firewall.
finding-github-unreachable-title = GitHub is not reachable
finding-immutable-distro-advice = Unilux writes only to your home directory, so this should work. Reports are welcome either way.
finding-immutable-distro-title = { $distro } is an immutable distribution
finding-log-certificate-advice = The patched libraries are probably not in use. Run a repair.
finding-log-certificate-title = Certificate errors in the launch log
finding-log-container-advice = Look at the line in the evidence; it often names a missing path or permission.
finding-log-container-title = Proton's container failed to start
finding-log-openxr-advice = Connect the headset before launching and check the runtime sees it.
finding-log-openxr-title = The game could not reach the OpenXR runtime
finding-log-tls-advice = The patched secur32/crypt32 are probably not in use. Run a repair.
finding-log-tls-title = TLS errors in the launch log
finding-log-vulkan-advice = Check the GPU driver and that Vulkan works (vulkaninfo).
finding-log-vulkan-title = Vulkan errors in the launch log
finding-no-gpu-title = No GPU found under /sys/class/drm
finding-no-patches-advice = Without it the launcher cannot sign in: stock Wine lacks the TLS client-certificate support Somnium needs.
finding-no-patches-title = No Somnium patch bundle is installed in this Proton
finding-no-proton-advice = A repair picks one.
finding-no-proton-title = No Proton version recorded
finding-no-vulkan-advice = Proton renders through Vulkan. Install your GPU's Vulkan driver (mesa-vulkan-drivers, vulkan-radeon, nvidia-utils, ...).
finding-no-vulkan-title = No Vulkan driver found
finding-openxr-override-advice = These settings replace detection entirely. If you need them, please report your runtime so detection can handle it.
finding-openxr-override-title = OpenXR detection is replaced by manual settings
finding-patches-intact-title = Patch bundle { $bundle } installed and intact
finding-patches-none-for-proton-advice = Switch to a verified Proton, or build a bundle with `unilux patch build --proton { $proton }` and test it.
finding-patches-none-for-proton-title = The catalog has no patch bundle for { $proton }
finding-patches-replaced-advice = Something (a Proton update, a manual copy) overwrote them. A repair puts them back.
finding-patches-replaced-title = Patched files from { $bundle } were replaced
finding-patches-untested-advice = It was built for a nearby Proton. If sign-in or video fails, switch to a verified Proton and report the result.
finding-patches-untested-title = The patch bundle for { $proton } is untested
finding-proton-missing-advice = A repair downloads it again.
finding-proton-missing-title = Proton is missing
finding-proton-too-old-advice = Proton 8 and older cannot initialise VR. Pick Proton 9 or newer in the Proton settings.
finding-proton-too-old-title = { $proton } is older than Proton 9
finding-python-missing-advice = { $hint ->
    [none] umu-run needs Python 3.10 or newer. Install it with your package manager.
   *[other] umu-run needs Python 3.10 or newer. Install it: { $hint }
    }
finding-python-missing-title = python3 is not installed
finding-python-old-advice = umu-run needs 3.10 or newer as python3 on your PATH. On older LTS releases this usually means upgrading the distribution.
finding-python-old-title = python3 is { $version }, older than 3.10
finding-somnium-missing-advice = Run the installer with Somnium's Windows installer from somniumspace.com.
finding-somnium-missing-title = Somnium Space is not installed in the prefix
finding-swap-disk-advice = Pages the game touches again come back from disk, and the frame waits for them: freezes when loading worlds and avatars. Set up zram (zram-generator or your distribution's zram package) so swapped pages stay in compressed RAM, and close browsers or other heavy apps before playing.
finding-swap-disk-title = The last session pushed { $gb } GB to swap
finding-swap-zram-advice = zram keeps swap cheap, but the kernel still evicted game memory. Close other heavy apps before playing; with zram, vm.swappiness between 100 and 180 swaps idle pages before the game's.
finding-swap-zram-title = The last session pushed { $gb } GB to zram
finding-umu-missing-advice = A repair downloads it again.
finding-umu-missing-title = umu-run is missing
finding-video-domain-blocked-advice = Somnium only plays links from domains on its own allow list; the player stays blank without an error. This is the game's rule, not Wine: use a YouTube link or a host the world's creator allows.
finding-video-domain-blocked-title = Somnium refused some video links
finding-video-extract-failed-advice = yt-dlp ran but could not read these links: private or age-restricted videos, or YouTube changed something. Try another video; if every one fails, Somnium needs a yt-dlp update.
finding-video-extract-failed-title = Some YouTube links could not be extracted
finding-vr-not-ready-title = VR is not ready
finding-vr-note-title = VR note
finding-vr-ready-title = VR ready: { $runtime }
finding-xr-overlay-advice = It is a second client of the compositor and takes focus from the game when shown. If slowdowns line up with it, close it to compare.
finding-xr-overlay-title = XR overlay running: { $overlays }
finding-ytdlp-blocked-advice = Somnium's yt-dlp.exe checks the name of its temporary directory, and stock Wine shortens it, so no YouTube video loads. Use a recipe with the pyinstaller-tempnam fix (the built-in recommended one has it): unilux recipe use recommended.
finding-ytdlp-blocked-title = yt-dlp cannot start under this Proton
fix-media-by-url-sum = Plays the live and web video streams that worlds use.
fix-media-by-url-title = Videos from links
fix-tls-client-certs-sum = Without it, signing in to Somnium never completes.
fix-tls-client-certs-title = Account sign-in
fix-ytdlp-android-client-sum = Picks a 360p stream that carries picture and sound together. Needs the YouTube downloader.
fix-ytdlp-android-client-title = YouTube with sound (obsolete)
fix-ytdlp-hook-sum = Lets Somnium fetch YouTube videos through yt-dlp.
